# The nested GPT inside userdata/linux names its partitions ESP and ARCH
# (CI parted `name`), so fstab uses PARTLABEL: no UUID placeholders, no
# fill step, and partition uevents give udev native symlinks without blkid
# probing (offset loops never got device units in the real root).
# Root fsck runs in the initramfs `fsck` hook (pass 0 here); first-boot
# grow is automatic (davinci-grow-rootfs.service: growpart p2 to fill the
# hosting partition + online resize2fs, stamped in
# /var/lib/davinci-grow-rootfs.done);
# /boot is best-effort (nofail) so a missing ESP can never strand login.
# <file system>   <mount point>  <type> <options>                          <dump> <pass>
PARTLABEL=ARCH  /              ext4   rw,errors=remount-ro,x-systemd.device-timeout=30  0 0
PARTLABEL=ESP   /boot          vfat   defaults,nofail,x-systemd.device-timeout=15       0 2
